ChoralRoot FM-1 0.39 – studio twin (firmware code for the host), built from https://github.com/Quixotic7/ChoralRootFM1 tag v0.39
(commit 36867e5c76fa1ecc02cba57102ee870695e1de10; source: https://github.com/Quixotic7/ChoralRootFM1/archive/36867e5c76fa1ecc02cba57102ee870695e1de10.tar.gz).
GPL-3.0-only. ChoralRoot FM-1 by Quixotic7 (ChoralRoot FM-1 contributors), a fork of Felucca: Copyright (C) 2026 Leo Kuroshita (@kurogedelic), Hügelton Instruments (Felucca);
the FM6, CZ-1 and Prophet-5 engines Melodee's, Copyright (C) 2026 Kerem Kilic (Ellic Studio); the others ChoralRoot's LICENSING.md names.
Ported parts keep their licences (msfa in fm6_core.c: Apache-2.0, Dexed: GPL-3.0-or-later; MAME's uPD933 in cz_native.c: BSD-3-Clause; felucca-bsp's fm1_flash_wait.h: MPL-2.0;
the UI face Inter Tight and the Fukiai icons are rasterised in: OFL 1.1, MIT): ChoralRoot's LICENSING.md and the texts in THIRD_PARTY.txt beside this file.
Casio's 64 CZ-1 preset tones and the Sequential Prophet-5 factory programs ChoralRoot ships are sound data, included as in ChoralRoot's own releases and browser emulator; their rights stay with Casio and Sequential.
The JieLi SDK files of ChoralRoot's packages and its Bluetooth stack are not part of the twin.
The firmware sources are unmodified. The glue tools/studio/choralroot_studio.c (GPL-3.0-only, in FM-1 Companion's source) includes them as ChoralRoot's own browser emulator and host tests do (tools/emu/web/emu_web.c,
tools/emu/emu_fw.c, tools/emu/emu_firmware.h, tests/cr_backup_test.c) and adds the USB SysEx path (usb.c, cr_backup.c's backup protocol, ota.c's identity handshake); the hardware stand-ins are the emulator's:
keys/LEDs/LCD, the key sensing, the MASTER pot, NOR flash = a 1 MiB RAM image, one core (the bass part's job runs inline), USB = always configured (SysEx and MIDI out through usb.c's rings),
no USB audio, no TRS MIDI, no Bluetooth, no serial console, no updater and no USB boot (ota.c answers the identity handshake only).
Compiled with WASI SDK clang (include shim tools/wasm_shim/sys/wait.h; tools/emu/web/compat from ChoralRoot's tree).

Corresponding Source (GNU GPL 3.0, section 6)
